{
 "rule": "R6, literal: the thresholds-only repair 'helps' on a log if its held-out D1 (heldout_disjoint, mean over the seeds of the complaint stream) after n = 10 reported complaints is at most 10 percent AND its Rel exact is within 2 points (absolute difference) of the deployed log's; the endpoint asks for this on both development logs (e2_curves) and on at least one mild prefix (this file).",
 "best_linear": "per log and n: the linear repair (COMP-B, COMP-B+, REEDIT-B, RB-TOT, RB-UNION) with the lowest mean held-out D1 over the seeds ('best_any'), and the lowest among those whose mean Rel exact is not more than 2 points below the deployed log ('best_rel': the one-sided selection of e2_curves/out/h1.json, adopted so that the prefix read-out is comparable with it; in favour of the baseline); the selection is made on the evaluation pool",
 "readings": "literal: |Rel - Rel deployed| <= 2 points (the verdict of this file); one-sided: Rel >= Rel deployed - 2 points (reported next to it, as e2_curves does); the two differ only where a repair has a higher Rel exact than the deployed log",
 "intervals": "paired crossed bootstrap over the 3 seeds of the complaint stream and the units (query clusters / edits), 2000 resamples",
